        Cell[CellGroupData[{Cell["C++ export and independent validation", "Subsection",
            ExpressionUUID -> "133f1c45-0fd1-4caf-88e8-4f261141d73b"], Cell["Run this cell after all \
helicity amplitudes above have completed successfully. One C++ class contains the complete helicity \
family. The saved Export variable keeps the build and both independent comparisons, including their \
random seeds. The final output is the generated directory on success; a failure remains visible.",
            "Text", ExpressionUUID -> "71e305c2-402b-4679-8c19-5db541adc7f0"],
           Cell["sm73Export = WriteSPINASProcess[\n  FileNameJoin[{spinasOutputDirectory, \
\"sm73_GGGG\"}],\n  {\"G\", \"G\"} -> {\"G\", \"G\"},\n  {\n  {{\"G.+\", \"G.+\", \"G.+\", \"G.+\"}, \
sm73PPPPAmplitude},\n  {{\"G.+\", \"G.+\", \"G.+\", \"G.-\"}, sm73PPPMAmplitude},\n  {{\"G.+\", \"G.+\", \
\"G.-\", \"G.+\"}, sm73PPMPAmplitude},\n  {{\"G.+\", \"G.+\", \"G.-\", \"G.-\"}, sm73PPMMAmplitude},\n  \
{{\"G.+\", \"G.-\", \"G.+\", \"G.+\"}, sm73PMPPAmplitude},\n  {{\"G.+\", \"G.-\", \"G.+\", \"G.-\"}, \
sm73PMPMAmplitude},\n  {{\"G.+\", \"G.-\", \"G.-\", \"G.+\"}, sm73PMMPAmplitude},\n  {{\"G.+\", \"G.-\", \
\"G.-\", \"G.-\"}, sm73PMMMAmplitude},\n  {{\"G.-\", \"G.+\", \"G.+\", \"G.+\"}, sm73MPPPAmplitude},\n  \
{{\"G.-\", \"G.+\", \"G.+\", \"G.-\"}, sm73MPPMAmplitude},\n  {{\"G.-\", \"G.+\", \"G.-\", \"G.+\"}, \
sm73MPMPAmplitude},\n  {{\"G.-\", \"G.+\", \"G.-\", \"G.-\"}, sm73MPMMAmplitude},\n  {{\"G.-\", \"G.-\", \
\"G.+\", \"G.+\"}, sm73MMPPAmplitude},\n  {{\"G.-\", \"G.-\", \"G.+\", \"G.-\"}, sm73MMPMAmplitude},\n  \
{{\"G.-\", \"G.-\", \"G.-\", \"G.+\"}, sm73MMMPAmplitude},\n  {{\"G.-\", \"G.-\", \"G.-\", \"G.-\"}, \
sm73MMMMAmplitude}\n  }, sm,\n  \"ProcessName\" -> \"sm73_GGGG\", Sequence @@ \
validationOptions];\nIf[AssociationQ[sm73Export], sm73Export[\"Directory\"], sm73Export]", "Input",
            ExpressionUUID -> "3bf0cf92-21a4-43b0-b1a0-0105a8709910"], Cell["Ten four-gluon helicity \
amplitudes vanish analytically. Numerical evaluation of the cancellations can leave a tiny residual. The \
MadGraph validator applies a 10^-22 absolute bound to exported exact-zero helicities and reports the \
measured residual and bound. The six nonzero helicities use the ordinary comparison.", "Text",
            CellTags -> "hepcat-gluon-exact-zero-replay", ExpressionUUID ->
             "d78619a2-e3b4-4cd6-b434-be445d2c6fc4"]}, Open]]}, Open]]}, Open]]},
